[[File:Jakku.png|thumb|right|250px|The desert landscape of the planet Jakku]]
{{Quote|Turns out it gets ''a lot hotter'' in the desert when the sun comes up.|[[Poe Dameron]]|<ref name="Poe Dameron 26">[[Poe Dameron 26|''Poe Dameron'' 26]]</ref>}}
'''Deserts''' were planetary regions covered almost completely by sparse terrain that received little precipitation. They were dry, desolate, and often harsh regions.<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> On [[Tatooine]], [[sandstorm]]s proved dangerous to local populations,<ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref> and some citizens worked as [[moisture farmer]]s to pump moisture from beneath the desert floor.<ref name="Episode IV" /> The [[planet]] [[Jakku]] also contained a desert.<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref> Both Tatooine<ref name="Episode IV" /> and Jakku had [[Color|golden]] tan sand.<ref name="Episode VII" /> Other examples of desert planets include [[Er'Kit]]<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> and [[Geonosis]].<ref name="AotC">{{Film|II}}</ref> [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], who hailed from Tatooine, thought of the desert as a merciless expanse that took everything from those who wandered it.<ref name="TCW Movie">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' film]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Deserts as whole were introduced in 1977 in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope'']] as [[Tatooine]]. It is the not only the first time deserts appear, but also the first climate to appear as well. The scenes for Tatooine in a [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope'']] were shot in [[Tunisia]].

